Installed by `sov connect claude-code` on {{DATE}}.

Write wire: `connectors/harness/claude-code/mirror.sh` every {{INTERVAL}}s via launchd
(`{{LABEL}}`), mirroring `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/` into `memory/<project>/`.
`memory/MANIFEST.md` is the heartbeat: last run, project count, failures.
Transcripts (`*.jsonl`) never cross.

Read wire: `connectors/harness/claude-code/session-start.sh`, registered as a
SessionStart hook in `~/.claude/settings.json`. It maps the session's working
directory to a workstream, runs `brain-load`, and injects the pack as context.
It never writes the pack into this lane or into Claude Code's memory files.
`brain-load-usage.md` here is its receipt, one line per session start.
